  "conclusion": "At 2\u03b1, 18/18 LLM \u00d7 method cells match or exceed their unsteered French-classifier retention and 18/18 exceed their matched-random mean on that diagnostic. Median cosine to the original French activation is 0.870, yet 18/18 have lower within-French geometry correlation than matched random; these semantic diagnostics remain representation-level proxies rather than generated-text evidence.",
  "entry_point": "experiments.exp07.report",
  "experiment_id": "exp07",
  "figures": [
    {
      "caption": "Gemma-2-2B held-out French activations receive the same train-selected, least-squares-calibrated English\u2192French vector again at m = 0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, and 2. Curves are means across three trained seeds with population-SD error bars. Purple identifies SSAEs and teal identifies SAEs; marker and dash identify variants. The neutral matched-random ribbon is the equal-weight mixture of 100 norm-matched directions per model/seed cell; the mean-difference control is train-derived. The broad unsteered reference is not uncertainty. The mean-difference control has zero off-axis drift by construction because it defines that reference axis. Paired retrieval, within-French geometry, and off-axis drift are representation-level proxies, not generated-text semantic evaluations.",
      "id": "target_overshoot_gemma",
      "title": "Gemma-2-2B target-side English\u2192French steering overshoot",
      "variants": [
        "figures/target-overshoot-gemma.pdf"
      ]
    },
    {
      "caption": "Pythia-70M held-out French activations receive the same train-selected, least-squares-calibrated English\u2192French vector again at m = 0, 0.25, 0.5, 1, and 2. Curves are means across three trained seeds with population-SD error bars. Purple identifies SSAEs and teal identifies SAEs; marker and dash identify variants. The neutral matched-random ribbon is the equal-weight mixture of 100 norm-matched directions per model/seed cell; the mean-difference control is train-derived. The broad unsteered reference is not uncertainty. The mean-difference control has zero off-axis drift by construction because it defines that reference axis. Paired retrieval, within-French geometry, and off-axis drift are representation-level proxies, not generated-text semantic evaluations.",
      "id": "target_overshoot_pythia",
      "title": "Pythia-70M target-side English\u2192French steering overshoot",
